# Instructions to Duplicate the GLB Avatar Button

This guide provides step-by-step instructions for an AI agent to duplicate the interactive `player-avatar-container` 3D GLB button within `NewOrigami.Panels.html`. 

## 1. HTML DOM Structure
Locate the existing avatar circle in the HTML and duplicate it with a new unique ID.

```html
<!-- Existing Button -->
<div class="avatar-circle" id="player-avatar-container" onclick="toggleRing()"></div>

<!-- NEW Duplicated Button -->
<div class="avatar-circle" id="secondary-avatar-container" onclick="customAction()"></div>
```

> [!TIP]
> The `.avatar-circle` CSS class automatically applies the neumorphic ring layout, 58x58px circular clipping bounds, and flexbox centering. You do not need to write new CSS unless you want different dimensions.

## 2. Declare New Global Three.js Variables
In the `<script type="module">` section where the existing avatar variables are declared, add a new set of independent variables for the secondary avatar.

```javascript
// Existing globals
let avatarMixer = null;
let avatarActions = {};
let avatarScene, avatarCamera, avatarRenderer;

// NEW globals for duplicated button
let secondaryAvatarMixer = null;
let secondaryAvatarActions = {};
let secondaryAvatarScene, secondaryAvatarCamera, secondaryAvatarRenderer;
```

## 3. Duplicate Initialization Logic
Locate the Three.js initialization block (where `avatarRenderer` is created). Duplicate this setup, swapping all references to point to the new variables and the new container ID.

```javascript
const container2 = document.getElementById('secondary-avatar-container');
if (container2) {
    const w = container2.clientWidth || 58;
    const h = container2.clientHeight || 58;

    // 1. Setup Renderer
    secondaryAvatarRenderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ alpha: true, antialias: false });
    secondaryAvatarRenderer.setClearColor(0x000000, 0); 
    secondaryAvatarRenderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 1.5));
    secondaryAvatarRenderer.setSize(w, h);
    container2.appendChild(secondaryAvatarRenderer.domElement);
    
    // 2. Setup Scene & Camera
    secondaryAvatarScene = new THREE.Scene();
    secondaryAvatarCamera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(40, w / h, 0.1, 100);
    secondaryAvatarCamera.position.set(0, 1.2, 4.8);
    secondaryAvatarCamera.lookAt(0, 0.85, 0);

    // 3. Add Lights
    const ambLight = new THREE.AmbientLight(0xffffff, 0.6);
    const dirLight = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 1.2);
    dirLight.position.set(2, 5, 3);
    secondaryAvatarScene.add(ambLight, dirLight);

    // 4. Load the GLB Model
    const loader = new GLTFLoader();
    loader.load('assets/models/YOUR_NEW_MODEL.glb', (gltf) => {
        const model = gltf.scene;
        // Apply optional scaling/positioning
        model.scale.set(1, 1, 1);
        model.position.set(0, 0, 0);
        secondaryAvatarScene.add(model);
        
        // 5. Setup Animation Mixer
        if (gltf.animations && gltf.animations.length) {
            secondaryAvatarMixer = new THREE.AnimationMixer(model);
            gltf.animations.forEach(anim => {
                const action = secondaryAvatarMixer.clipAction(anim);
                secondaryAvatarActions[anim.name.toLowerCase()] = action;
            });
            // Play default animation
            if (secondaryAvatarActions['idle']) secondaryAvatarActions['idle'].play();
        }
    });
}
```

## 4. Hook into the Unified Render Loop
Finally, locate the `renderLoop(time)` function. You must update the new mixer with the existing `delta` time, and tell the new renderer to draw the scene so the button stays animated.

```javascript
function renderLoop(time) {
    requestAnimationFrame(renderLoop);
    
    // Throttle to 30 FPS logic (already exists)
    if (time - lastRender < 33) return;
    lastRender = time;
    const delta = avatarClock.getDelta(); // Reuse existing clock

    // Existing update
    if (avatarMixer) avatarMixer.update(delta);
    if (avatarRenderer) avatarRenderer.render(avatarScene, avatarCamera);

    // NEW update logic for duplicate
    if (secondaryAvatarMixer) {
        secondaryAvatarMixer.update(delta);
    }
    
    if (secondaryAvatarRenderer && secondaryAvatarScene && secondaryAvatarCamera) {
        // Apply resize logic here if container dynamically scales
        secondaryAvatarRenderer.render(secondaryAvatarScene, secondaryAvatarCamera);
    }
}
```
